@@ -0,0 +1,77 @@
+# USDC Pay
+
+A small dApp for sending **USDC on Ethereum mainnet**. Connect a wallet, see
+your USDC and ETH balances, enter a recipient and amount, and send.
+
+The token is the real Circle USDC contract on mainnet:
+`0xA0b86991c6218b36c1d19D4a2e9Eb0cE3606eB48` (6 decimals).
+
+## Stack
+
+Production-standard Ethereum frontend stack:
+
+- **Next.js 14** (App Router) + **TypeScript**
+- **wagmi v2** + **viem v2** — typed contract reads/writes
+- **RainbowKit** — wallet connection UI (MetaMask, Coinbase, WalletConnect, …)
+- **TanStack Query** — caching / background refresh (wired in by wagmi)
+
+## Getting started
+
+```bash
+npm install
+cp .env.example .env.local   # then fill in the values
+npm run dev                  # http://localhost:3000  → redirects to /pay
+```
+
+### Environment
+
+| Variable | Required | Purpose |
+| --- | --- | --- |
+| `NEXT_PUBLIC_WALLETCONNECT_PROJECT_ID` | recommended | Enables WalletConnect (mobile / QR wallets). Get one free at [cloud.reown.com](https://cloud.reown.com). Injected wallets like MetaMask work without it. |
+| `NEXT_PUBLIC_MAINNET_RPC_URL` | recommended | A dedicated mainnet RPC (Alchemy/Infura/…). Falls back to a public RPC if unset — fine for local dev, not for production traffic. |
+
+## Scripts
+
+- `npm run dev` — dev server
+- `npm run build` — production build
+- `npm run start` — serve the production build
+- `npm run typecheck` — `tsc --noEmit`
+- `npm run lint` — ESLint (Next core-web-vitals)
+
+## How it works
+
+- **`/pay`** (`src/app/pay/page.tsx`) is the only surface; `/` redirects to it.
+- **Balances** (`src/components/BalancePanel.tsx`)
+  - USDC via `balanceOf` (`src/hooks/useUsdcBalance.ts`)
+  - ETH via wagmi's native `useBalance`
+  - Both refresh every ~15s; a warning shows when ETH is 0 (no gas).
+- **Sending** (`src/components/PayForm.tsx`)
+  - Calls the ERC-20 `transfer(recipient, amount)` via `useWriteContract`.
+  - Waits for the receipt with `useWaitForTransactionReceipt` and shows
+    signing → sending → confirmed states with an Etherscan link.
+
+### Correctness notes (why USDC is handled "faithfully")
+
+- **6 decimals, not 18.** Amounts are parsed with `parseUnits(amount, 6)` and
+  the on-chain `decimals()` is also read as a cross-check. The input rejects
+  more than 6 fractional digits. (See `src/lib/usdc.ts`, `src/lib/format.ts`.)
+- **Checksummed address.** The contract address is normalized with viem's
+  `getAddress`.
+- **Mainnet-only.** USDC at this address is only the real token on mainnet, so
+  the app is configured for chain id 1 and blocks/offers-to-switch on any other
+  network (`src/components/NetworkGuard.tsx`).
+- **Input guards.** Recipient must be a valid, non-zero address; amount must be
+  > 0 and within the current USDC balance before the button enables.
+- **Human-readable failures.** Common wallet/RPC errors (user rejection,
+  insufficient gas, insufficient balance) are mapped to plain-language messages.
+
+## Notes & trade-offs
+
+- No approvals are needed: a direct `transfer` moves the sender's own USDC.
+  (Approve/`transferFrom` would only matter for a contract spending on the
+  user's behalf, which this app doesn't do.)
+- The build aliases some optional `@x402/*` payment packages to `false` in
+  `next.config.mjs`. They are lazy, unused optional deps of the Coinbase/Base
+  connector that RainbowKit bundles; they are not installed and not needed here.
+- Mainnet-only by design — there's no testnet mode, since the task is about the
+  real token.
diff --git a/next.config.mjs b/next.config.mjs
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..6d5e3fd
--- /dev/null
+++ b/next.config.mjs
@@ -0,0 +1,25 @@
+/** @type {import('next').NextConfig} */
+const nextConfig = {
+  reactStrictMode: true,
+  webpack: (config) => {
+    // Silence optional-dependency warnings from WalletConnect / MetaMask SDK.
+    config.externals.push("pino-pretty", "lokijs", "encoding");
+
+    // The Coinbase/Base account connector (pulled in by RainbowKit's default
+    // wallet list) lazily imports optional "x402" payment packages that we
+    // never use. They are not installed, so resolve them to `false` instead
+    // of failing the build.
+    config.resolve.alias = {
+      ...config.resolve.alias,
+      "@x402/evm": false,
+      "@x402/evm/exact/client": false,
+      "@x402/evm/upto/client": false,
+      "@x402/svm/exact/client": false,
+      "@x402/core/client": false,
+    };
+
+    return config;
+  },
+};
+
+export default nextConfig;
